WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:01.830
- So the question is will Donald Trump

00:00:01.830 --> 00:00:03.720
be able to maintain all of the benefits

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:06.260
of being a President
when he leaves office?

00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:07.330
Things like a pension,

00:00:07.330 --> 00:00:10.480
things like a secret service
detachment to protect him.

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:13.370
Well, the answer is maybe, but probably.

00:00:13.370 --> 00:00:16.100
A lot of this is defined by
the Former Presidents Act,

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:18.910
which defines a former
President as someone

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:20.670
who shall have held
the office of President

00:00:20.670 --> 00:00:21.910
of the United States of America

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:24.450
and whose service in such office
shall have been terminated

00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:26.010
other than by removal pursuant

00:00:26.010 --> 00:00:28.000
to Section Four of Article
Two of the Constitution.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:29.660
So, in other words, you
get all the benefits

00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:31.010
of the Former Presidents Act

00:00:31.010 --> 00:00:33.260
so long as you weren't removed pursuant

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:35.110
to a trial after impeachment.

00:00:35.110 --> 00:00:36.940
So it seems like if Donald Trump resigned,

00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:39.480
he'd still get the benefits
of the Former Presidents Act

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:40.860
and he'd get all of those benefits

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:43.620
so long as he isn't removed pursuant

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:45.650
to the Senate trial of impeachment,

00:00:45.650 --> 00:00:48.810
and as I've covered before,
that seems incredibly unlikely.

00:00:48.810 --> 00:00:50.490
Fellow legal commentator, Richard Hoeg,

00:00:50.490 --> 00:00:51.860
has done a whole video about it

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:52.970
and he goes into great detail

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:54.110
about the Former Presidents Act.

00:00:54.110 --> 00:00:55.210
I recommend you check it out,

00:00:55.210 --> 00:00:57.743
and there's always, I'll see you in court.

